## Caveats for teaching

- `date` is the field **end** date; a poll fielded over a long period (some
  span weeks) is dated at its close.
- Because universes (LV/RV/A) are mixed and pollsters vary, day-to-day
  volatility includes sampling error — good material for the polling-accuracy
  lecture.
- Spot values verified against the source tables (e.g. Marist 11/3/2008
  Obama 52 / McCain 43; Bloomberg 11/6/2016 Clinton 46 / Trump 43).
